<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Njeri used the expansion of <m>(1 + x)^{5}</m> to estimate <m>{0.98}^{5}</m> correct to 4 decimal places. Her working has one mistake.</p><ol><li><m>{0.98} = 1 + x</m> with <m>x = -{0.02}</m>.</li><li>The row for power <m>{5}</m> starts <m>1, {4}, {6}, {4}</m>.</li><li><m>x^2 = {0.0004}</m>, <m>x^3 = {-0.000008}</m>.</li><li>The first four terms are <m>1, {-0.08}, {0.0024}, {-0.000032}</m>.</li><li>Their sum is <m>{0.922368}</m>.</li><li>So <m>{0.98}^{5} \approx {0.9224}</m>.</li></ol><p>(a) Which step has the mistake?</p><div>[ Step 1 | Step 2 | Step 3 | Step 4 | Step 5 | Step 6 ]  </div><p>(b) Give the correct value of <m>{0.98}^{5}</m>, correct to 4 decimal places.</p><div><fillin characters="10" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Check each step: the row of Pascal's triangle, the powers of <m>x</m> (a square has twice as many decimal places as the number), and the sign of each term (odd powers of a negative number are negative).</p><p>(a) The mistake is in Step 2: <m>1, {4}, {6}, {4}</m> starts the row for power <m>{4}</m>. The row for power <m>{5}</m> starts <m>1, {5}, {10}, {10}</m>.</p><p>(b) Done correctly: <m>x = -{0.02}</m>, the row starts <m>1, {5}, {10}, {10}</m>, <m>x^2 = {0.0004}</m>, <m>x^3 = {-0.000008}</m>, the terms are <m>1, {-0.1}, {0.004}, {-0.00008}</m>, their sum is <m>{0.90392}</m>, so <m>{0.98}^{5} \approx {0.9039}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>Step 2</p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{11299}{12500}</m></p></answer>
